1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,520
♪ I've never believed in love ♪

2
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:16,920
♪ I've never trusted anyone ♪

3
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:19,600
♪ I've always lived by reason ♪

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,920
♪ I've never followed my heart ♪

5
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:27,080
♪ Locked away with a complicated code ♪

6
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:31,560
♪ But you broke through
My heavily guarded firewall ♪

7
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:35,720
♪ That used to protect my heart ♪

8
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:40,600
♪ I'm in love with you ♪

9
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,200
♪ I've just realized today that love ♪

10
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:50,240
♪ Is something I should get to know and explore ♪

11
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:53,600
♪ The code to my heart has been cracked ♪

12
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,720
♪ By the love you wrapped me in ♪

13
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:00,360
♪ Having you close puts you in my dreams ♪

14
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,720
♪ You're always on my mind ♪

15
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:04,400
♪ You cracked my code ♪

16
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:07,600
♪ My heart's security system is disabled ♪

17
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:10,800
♪ You unlocked my heart with a love ♪

18
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,440
♪ That this world has never given me ♪

19
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:18,160
♪ Can I write a new code ♪

20
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:20,920
♪ That says I love you? ♪

21
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,600
♪ Love you ♪

22
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:35,800
My future wife went after your boyfriend?

23
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,200
I am Kit’s fiancé.

24
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:40,120
Once my son has recovered,

25
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,680
I will hold the wedding immediately.

26
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,400
I can handle my problems by myself!

27
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,720
You can't handle your problems!

28
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:47,720
That's why I decided to marry you!

29
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:52,240
You see the power going out

30
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,280
as bad omen.

31
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:56,480
But for me, it's a fortunate thing.

32
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,400
So we're really going to be living here.

33
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:13,800
A normal human heart beats

34
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,680
60 to 100 times per minute.

35
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:18,440
Mine is beating at 85 per minute

36
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:19,480
I'm healthy.

37
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,120
Nothing concerning.

38
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,240
It's hot.

39
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:36,880
At certain times,

40
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,760
my heart pounds really hard.

41
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:56,560
What are you looking at?

42
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,280
It's nothing.

43
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,760
Hand me the air conditioner remote.

44
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:03,520
Oh, alright.

45
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:15,920
Why are your hands shaking?

46
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:19,760
I was carrying heavy stuff.

47
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:20,680
Hey, no.

48
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,200
Whoa.

49
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,400
Why is it so high, Nont?

50
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:26,160
You should go rest, I'll handle the rest.

51
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,480
I'm totally fine,

52
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:28,680
I was just carrying heavy stuff.

53
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,760
Don't be stubborn.

54
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:30,680
Kit!

55
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,560
Kit, I...

56
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,080
Kit!

57
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,400
You rest well, I'll go buy dinner.

58
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,360
so you don't have to

59
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,560
tire yourself out cooking.

60
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:52,840
Alright.

61
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:58,480
Sleep.

62
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:15,160
I didn't know what it was back then.

63
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:17,960
I only knew that every time

64
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:19,280
my heart starts racing,

65
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,720
Kit is always close by.

66
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,360
It started 10 years ago.

67
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,160
Kit,

68
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,480
(Highschool Student)
what kind of brother are you

69
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,800
to let your brother come home

70
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,040
in such a condition?

71
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,840
Auntie, Kit has nothing to do with this,

72
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,560
I was just careless.

73
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:38,640
First day at school

74
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:39,840
and there's already trouble.

75
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,520
If your little brother

76
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:43,000
comes home like this again,

77
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,640
I'll deduct your allowance.

78
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:46,080
Mom, you're worried about Nont,

79
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,320
but you're directing it at me.

80
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,040
It's not fair.

81
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,520
How is it not fair?

82
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:50,600
You're the elder brother,

83
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,760
you have the duty to look after your brother.

84
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,520
But I'm your only son, Mom.

85
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:04,480
How much allowance do you get per month?

86
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,160
3,000 baht.

87
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,760
I'll deduct your allowance

88
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,720
down to 2,500 baht.

89
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:12,520
Mom, that's my lunch money.

90
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,760
Then don't eat,

91
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:15,280
so you can go on a diet too.

92
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:18,000
But I'm an athlete, I need my protein.

93
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,360
You can have a boiled egg.

94
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,160
It's cheap and has a lot of protein.

95
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,840
Mom, I love Nont,

96
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,800
but I can't watch him 24 hours a day.

97
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,040
It's impossible.

98
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,640
I'm not telling you to watch him

99
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,200
I'm saying you have to look after him.

100
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:38,400
Alright.

101
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,200
Nont, from now on,

102
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:46,360
you have to come and return home with me.

103
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,360
Got it?

104
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:52,120
I'm not angry at you.

105
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,160
I understand.

106
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:59,800
Nont, if you have something on your mind,

107
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:02,120
just tell him directly.

108
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:03,520
Yes, Auntie.

109
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,480
And as for you, Kit...

110
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:07,760
"Take care of Nont." Yes, I know.

111
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:10,440
If you know, then do it.

112
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:20,040
But this month's allowance

113
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,120
is still 3,000 baht.

114
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:24,160
But if your brother comes home

115
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,600
in this condition again,

116
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,880
I'll deduct 500 baht for each mark.

117
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,440
You really dare to argue with Auntie?

118
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,280
It has to happen sometimes,

119
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:45,040
or else I wouldn't be able to have lunch.

120
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:46,760
Kit.

121
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,200
I'm sorry for making you get scolded.

122
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:59,920
Go get changed
and meet me at the swimming pool.

123
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,720
Why?

124
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,400
I'll teach you self-defense,

125
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,600
so I won't have to lose 500 baht per mark.

126
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:13,400
Go.

127
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,320
One, two.

128
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,720
Are you scared that it'll get hurt? Do it hard.

129
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:23,360
One, two.

130
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,280
One, two.

131
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,200
Put some effort into it.

132
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:28,760
Look at the target clearly.

133
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:29,440
Yes.

134
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:30,720
One, two.

135
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,840
Oh!

136
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,760
This is the first time

137
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,720
my heart has raced this hard.

138
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:40,040
It only gets stronger

139
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:42,160
the closer we are.

140
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,400
Are you okay?

141
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:45,120
Yes.

142
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,920
I've diagnosed myself.

143
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,720
I'm falling in love.

144
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,560
One, two.

145
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:55,880
and there's no medical cure for it yet.

146
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:02,400
(First year of university)

147
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,320
So,

148
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,440
how did you injure your hand boxing?

149
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,080
I was falling,

150
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,440
so I put my hand out to break the fall.

151
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:12,320
And how are you going to shower?

152
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,160
I'll use my right hand.

153
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,480
Turn around.

154
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:44,840
It's normal.

155
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,360
It's normal.

156
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,080
It's normal.

157
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,680
It's normal.

158
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:03,160
It's normal.

159
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,480
Dang.

160
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:12,080
It's not normal at all!

161
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,120
Oh.

162
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,840
Does it hurt?

163
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:25,680
Umm...

164
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,560
Your hands are cold.

165
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:30,560
Cold?

166
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,080
Turn around.

167
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,560
Turn around.

168
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:41,440
I said turn around.

169
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,520
Don't look at his lips.

170
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,760
Don't look at his lips.

171
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:11,480
Don't look at his lips.

172
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,000
I'm looking at it!

173
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:16,120
Why is your face red?

174
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,240
Your hands are cold.

175
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:20,840
Oh.

176
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:22,360
Your hands are hot.

177
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:24,360
Are they hot or cold?

178
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:27,040
Hot.

179
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,800
Let me wash you up in a bit.

180
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,080
Uh... Kit, I'm already clean.

181
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,400
Okay.

182
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:06,520
Come out when you're done.

183
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:07,680
I'll dry you off.

184
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:18,440
Thank you.

185
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:28,800
That was the first time

186
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,400
I realized that I love Kit,

187
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,720
not just as a brother.

188
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:36,920
But I'm scared that

189
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:39,040
if he knew,

190
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:41,960
would he look at me the same way?

191
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:47,520
Nont.

192
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,080
Having a good dream?

193
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:04,800
I was dreaming of you.

194
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:07,720
Did you know

195
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,080
I miss you too?

196
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,040
Thank you for

197
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:14,920
taking care of me in every way.

198
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,120
Kit.

199
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,400
What are you afraid of?

200
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:33,560
I'm scared of waking up.

201
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:37,240
Then don't wake up.

202
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,080
Nont!

203
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:03,880
Are you feeling better?

204
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,080
I'm okay now.

205
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:09,560
Then I'll set the table.

206
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:14,640
Why didn't you cover yourself with a blanket?

207
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:17,760
You'll get sick.

208
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,120
When I'm done setting the table,
come eat when you're ready.

209
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:48,320
After all this time,

210
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,840
I never told Kit how I feel.

211
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:54,400
Because if I told him and he backed away,

212
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,640
I wouldn't even have this spot left.

213
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,240
Hey!

214
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:40,680
What is it, Nont?

215
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:42,400
- Do you have a cramp?
- Wake up, wake up.

216
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:43,200
Do you have a cramp?

217
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:45,200
No, I forgot that we have

218
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,800
a meal with Mama Wan today.

219
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:47,680
That's it?

220
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:49,640
Just move it to another day,
tell her I'm not available.

221
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:53,160
No, you have to wake up, Kit.

222
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:55,560
Mama Wan already made
an appointment, we must go.

223
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:57,200
If I go and you don't,

224
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:59,920
I'll trick her into giving
all her inheritance to me.

225
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Kit!

226
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,440
Kit!

227
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,200
When the time comes,

228
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:09,400
I'll order you around for everything.

229
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,560
Fine, I'm up.

230
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:13,080
Go shower.

231
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:19,880
Dress up nicely today, please.

232
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:24,280
Nont, where are my long-sleeved shirts?

233
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,640
I can't find them.

234
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:27,800
I put them in the other closet for you.

235
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:29,040
The left closet?

236
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:30,160
Wait, no, Kit!

237
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:32,480
That's not it! That's mine!
I will grab it for you!

238
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,200
Ugh.

239
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,560
This closet isn't organized it yet.

240
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:38,040
There wasn't time to sort it.

241
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,280
Kit, what are you laughing at?

242
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:44,040
How could I not laugh?

243
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,400
You organized my closet so neatly

244
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:47,080
then look at your own. It's a mess.

245
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:49,240
Umm...

246
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,360
Kit,

247
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,480
look at my eyes.

248
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,720
What?

249
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:54,640
You see...

250
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:56,400
I...

251
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:00,920
Mmm.

252
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:02,960
Is this style comfortable to wear?

253
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:05,960
Umm...

254
00:16:06,560 --> 00:16:08,720
I wear it for working out.

255
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,680
It supports well.

256
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,480
Supports well...

257
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:13,800
- Should I try one too?
- Oh.

258
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:17,160
I can't recommend it for you, either.

259
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:19,080
It's your personal preference.

260
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,040
Okay.

261
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:33,520
As for yours, Kit,

262
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:35,520
I had the chef prepare steak and fried eggs,

263
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:37,600
the way you liked them when you were little.

264
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:39,760
But I don't eat...

265
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,280
Yes. Thank you.

266
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:50,680
And for you, Nont, no MSG at all.

267
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:53,120
This is fried Chinese sausage,

268
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:55,000
salted fish salad, pickled mustard greens,

269
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,200
and salted egg salad.

270
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:59,560
Thank you, Mama Wan. You're the best.

271
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,640
Come on, let's eat then.

272
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:10,800
Eat a lot, okay?

273
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:11,720
Yes.

274
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,560
Kit,

275
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,360
Mom has something important
I want to talk to you about.

276
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:24,840
Whenever you're free,

277
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:26,280
come talk to me, okay?

278
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,720
Let me say this upfront,

279
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:31,600
if it's about me coming back
to help with the business...

280
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:32,680
I'm not ready yet.

281
00:17:34,280 --> 00:17:36,120
Then when will you be ready?

282
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,320
Do I have to wait until I go to see Indra first?

283
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,040
It's just that I have work to do.

284
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:41,480
Non.

285
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:43,720
Stop kicking my leg.

286
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:56,320
Excuse me.

287
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,720
Hello, Nu.

288
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:00,720
Hey, Kit.

289
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,560
Roch wants to talk to you privately.

290
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,280
I think

291
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:08,120
you should go talk it out and clear things up

292
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,720
before making any decisions.

293
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:11,680
I don't like this approach at all.

294
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,280
I know.

295
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:16,120
I'm just afraid of out of the frying pan,
into the fire.

296
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:17,560
Someone like Roch

297
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:19,400
is probably easier to read.

298
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:21,080
Okay, I understand.

299
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:23,680
Please help me set up the meeting.

300
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:25,680
Mm.

301
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:26,840
Alright.

302
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:34,160
I actually have something to
take care of at the office.

303
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:35,320
Please excuse me.

304
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,320
Haa...

305
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,440
A mother and son having conversation,

306
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:47,680
does it have to be this hard? Huh?

307
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:04,480
Please have a seat.

308
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:13,320
Thanks for agreeing to meet.

309
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:17,360
Nu said you had something personal to discuss.

310
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,680
How long has it been since
we last met like this?

311
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,480
It hasn't been that long.

312
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:26,440
But the real question is why
we never needed to meet like this at all.

313
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:28,680
That's why I wanted to clear the air with you.

314
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,600
Clear the air about what?

315
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:31,880
About what made us stop talking.

316
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:34,800
I'm graduating next term.

317
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:36,320
I'm going back to Thailand.

318
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,760
Why the sudden change of plans?

319
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,200
Someone's waiting for me.

320
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,640
Who? Can you tell me?

321
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:41,520
My little brother.

322
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:44,120
Your brother? Back home?

323
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,080
Yeah.

324
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:48,600
Like a brother, but not by blood.

325
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,840
At least you were honest with me.

326
00:19:57,680 --> 00:20:00,000
Before you leave, let me treat you to a meal.

327
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,040
Sure thing.

328
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:02,440
After exams, let's set it up.

329
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:16,920
You're really not staying
to further your studies?

330
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:18,720
I want to go back and work.

331
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:21,600
Once I finish my doctorate,
let's go back together.

332
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:24,040
Please? Can you do that?

333
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:29,280
Roch, get some sleep first.

334
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:31,400
Wait.

335
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:33,400
Don't leave yet.

336
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:38,080
I love you, Kit.

337
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:41,160
I love you so much.

338
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:43,320
I don't see you that way.

339
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:47,200
Just give me a chance.

340
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:53,640
Kit.

341
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:55,640
Roch, stop!

342
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,360
Kit.

343
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,120
I'm sorry.

344
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:13,400
Kit.

345
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,240
Kit!

346
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:15,800
Kit!

347
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,280
Did you know how
I felt about you back then,

348
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:23,520
when we were over there?

349
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:24,680
I was starting to figure it out.

350
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:26,320
Then why didn't you say anything?

351
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:27,920
Because I didn't have an answer for you.

352
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:29,400
Do you have one now?

353
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:30,880
I'm still learning about myself.

354
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:34,080
But there's one thing I know for sure.

355
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:36,720
The reason I didn't answer you back then

356
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:38,280
wasn't because I didn't want to,

357
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:40,400
it's because I didn't feel the way you felt.

358
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:43,480
For what I did that day, I'm sorry.

359
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,040
Okay.

360
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,600
And...

361
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:54,040
now that we're working together,

362
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:55,120
are you okay with that?

363
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,680
That depends on what you're here as.

364
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,040
A business partner.

365
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:00,560
Only that.

366
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:03,800
But I still enjoy a good competition.

367
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:04,880
That part, I understand.

368
00:22:54,296 --> 00:22:55,496
Mama Wan.

369
00:22:55,976 --> 00:22:56,456
Hmm?

370
00:22:56,456 --> 00:22:58,856
Can I ask you something?

371
00:22:59,176 --> 00:23:00,456
Of course, dear.

372
00:23:00,456 --> 00:23:03,576
Why did you have to
buy a house for Nont and me too?

373
00:23:04,696 --> 00:23:07,656
I think just holding the wedding

374
00:23:07,656 --> 00:23:08,816
would be enough

375
00:23:08,816 --> 00:23:10,576
to keep the other side from interfering.

376
00:23:15,576 --> 00:23:17,016
I want Kit to have a space

377
00:23:17,016 --> 00:23:18,696
where he feels at ease.

378
00:23:19,416 --> 00:23:21,736
I've been his mother for 27 years.

379
00:23:22,376 --> 00:23:23,856
Sometimes I think

380
00:23:24,736 --> 00:23:27,016
he just needs time and space.

381
00:23:27,736 --> 00:23:29,016
What do you mean, Mama Wan?

382
00:23:29,576 --> 00:23:31,536
I just hope that

383
00:23:32,456 --> 00:23:34,416
the person beside him

384
00:23:35,576 --> 00:23:36,816
will help him

385
00:23:37,136 --> 00:23:39,336
find his own answers one day.

386
00:23:44,536 --> 00:23:46,496
Liquidity is tighter than expected, sir.

387
00:23:47,216 --> 00:23:50,216
The revolving credit line might not be enough
to cover the next payment round.

388
00:23:50,216 --> 00:23:52,456
And if news leaks while
investors are watching,

389
00:23:52,456 --> 00:23:54,376
we could be hit on stability.

390
00:23:54,976 --> 00:23:55,976
What are the employees saying?

391
00:23:55,976 --> 00:23:58,576
Some teams are starting to
worry about salaries.

392
00:23:58,576 --> 00:24:00,576
If we don't manage confidence now,

393
00:24:00,576 --> 00:24:02,736
it could affect the company's image.

394
00:24:05,176 --> 00:24:07,816
Go gather all the job applications
and bring them to me.

395
00:24:07,816 --> 00:24:10,336
Mr. Roch, are we hiring more staff?

396
00:24:10,656 --> 00:24:12,176
We need to make it look like

397
00:24:12,176 --> 00:24:13,416
we're still growing.

398
00:24:13,936 --> 00:24:14,936
Understood.

399
00:24:30,376 --> 00:24:33,056
Nontawat Auttawarakul.

400
00:24:35,136 --> 00:24:36,376
Same surname as Kit.

401
00:24:42,896 --> 00:24:44,776
Schedule an interview with Mr. Nontawat.

402
00:24:44,776 --> 00:24:45,736
As soon as possible.

403
00:24:45,736 --> 00:24:46,816
Understood, sir.

404
00:25:00,216 --> 00:25:01,096
Nontawat.

405
00:25:02,176 --> 00:25:03,216
Auttawarakul.

406
00:25:19,536 --> 00:25:20,616
Morning, boss.

407
00:25:21,016 --> 00:25:22,936
Mr. Roch from RC Capital has arrived.

408
00:25:22,936 --> 00:25:24,136
Panu is waiting as well.

409
00:25:24,136 --> 00:25:25,696
He came early?

410
00:25:25,696 --> 00:25:26,736
Yes.

411
00:25:27,096 --> 00:25:28,896
Would you like me to join the meeting, boss?

412
00:25:28,896 --> 00:25:30,896
Come along. You can help catch the ball.

413
00:25:30,896 --> 00:25:31,896
Yes, sir.

414
00:25:36,616 --> 00:25:37,856
He should be here soon.

415
00:25:47,216 --> 00:25:48,376
Kit.

416
00:25:48,376 --> 00:25:49,736
Roch.

417
00:25:49,736 --> 00:25:51,416
Roch has an additional proposal.

418
00:25:51,416 --> 00:25:53,096
He wanted to talk before we proceed.

419
00:25:53,096 --> 00:25:54,216
Sure.

420
00:25:54,216 --> 00:25:56,936
Today, may I speak owner to owner?

421
00:26:10,856 --> 00:26:12,376
First give me a summary,

422
00:26:13,096 --> 00:26:14,696
why is NSL worth investing in?

423
00:26:15,216 --> 00:26:16,616
We do data analytic.

424
00:26:17,216 --> 00:26:18,696
We help large organizations use data

425
00:26:18,696 --> 00:26:19,736
to generate revenue.

426
00:26:19,736 --> 00:26:22,416
In the future, every business
will have to work with AI.

427
00:26:22,416 --> 00:26:23,656
We help them get ready.

428
00:26:24,016 --> 00:26:25,096
Very good.

429
00:26:26,496 --> 00:26:28,296
But the investors I'll be talking to,

430
00:26:28,736 --> 00:26:30,056
they only care about one thing,

431
00:26:31,216 --> 00:26:33,256
how to make the stock go up.

432
00:26:33,256 --> 00:26:36,136
I understand. That's your job, Roch.

433
00:26:37,256 --> 00:26:38,536
Here's the thing, Kit.

434
00:26:38,536 --> 00:26:39,816
NSL's new project,

435
00:26:39,816 --> 00:26:41,896
the new investors are fine with everything.

436
00:26:42,496 --> 00:26:45,096
But Roch wants a co-executive position.

437
00:26:46,816 --> 00:26:48,456
About the position, I'm not opposed.

438
00:26:48,776 --> 00:26:51,336
But operational decisions
have to come from our side.

439
00:26:52,416 --> 00:26:54,096
Kit, you don't have to be so tense.

440
00:26:55,376 --> 00:26:57,256
If I could do this alone,

441
00:26:57,256 --> 00:26:58,576
I wouldn't need to merge with you.

442
00:27:00,816 --> 00:27:02,056
And more importantly,

443
00:27:02,056 --> 00:27:04,256
I definitely won't bring up the past.

444
00:27:07,376 --> 00:27:09,496
How about this? Our company's image,

445
00:27:09,496 --> 00:27:11,016
we can adjust that together.

446
00:27:11,856 --> 00:27:14,016
But for NSL's new project,

447
00:27:14,016 --> 00:27:15,896
I'll let Kit form a new team

448
00:27:15,896 --> 00:27:17,216
right after the merger is announced.

449
00:27:19,616 --> 00:27:21,616
Consider it a gentleman's agreement, then.

450
00:27:22,456 --> 00:27:24,256
If it goes according to the agreement,

451
00:27:24,896 --> 00:27:25,976
I'm fine with it.

452
00:27:42,056 --> 00:27:43,456
Glad to be working together.

453
00:28:01,576 --> 00:28:03,056
Nu, are you sure this is a good idea?

454
00:28:04,016 --> 00:28:05,256
Good or not,

455
00:28:05,256 --> 00:28:06,656
I'm not sure.

456
00:28:06,656 --> 00:28:07,816
But if our company

457
00:28:07,816 --> 00:28:09,296
doesn't get new investors,

458
00:28:10,856 --> 00:28:12,456
we might never reach our dream.

459
00:28:38,536 --> 00:28:39,576
Kit.

460
00:28:49,976 --> 00:28:51,296
Drink some alkaline water first.

461
00:28:52,256 --> 00:28:53,856
That way you won't be sore tomorrow.

462
00:29:09,576 --> 00:29:11,616
Was there something stressful at the office?

463
00:29:11,616 --> 00:29:12,856
Something like that.

464
00:29:14,496 --> 00:29:15,616
Then

465
00:29:15,616 --> 00:29:17,416
want me to help relieve your stress?

466
00:29:21,496 --> 00:29:24,136
Sure. Go all out, then.

467
00:29:24,136 --> 00:29:25,416
Just try to keep up, then.

468
00:29:27,256 --> 00:29:29,416
Whoa, you know my moves too?

469
00:29:29,416 --> 00:29:30,456
Of course.

470
00:29:30,456 --> 00:29:31,376
Come on.

471
00:29:32,336 --> 00:29:33,816
Oh ho,

472
00:29:33,816 --> 00:29:34,856
not bad at all.

473
00:29:38,896 --> 00:29:40,056
Hey!

474
00:29:44,456 --> 00:29:46,296
If that had landed, I'd have been out cold.

475
00:29:46,296 --> 00:29:48,016
Luck was on my side today.

476
00:29:48,496 --> 00:29:50,216
If I'd known you'd climb over me like this,

477
00:29:50,216 --> 00:29:51,296
I wouldn't have taught you boxing.

478
00:29:51,296 --> 00:29:52,456
Too late.

479
00:29:54,256 --> 00:29:55,416
Come on.

480
00:29:55,936 --> 00:29:56,936
Come on.

481
00:29:59,416 --> 00:30:02,336
Hey! Fast, fast, fast!

482
00:30:02,336 --> 00:30:03,456
Come on.

483
00:30:19,816 --> 00:30:20,936
Kit.

484
00:30:20,936 --> 00:30:21,936
Hmm?

485
00:30:22,576 --> 00:30:24,456
I have finished my master's degree.

486
00:30:25,136 --> 00:30:26,616
Let me apply for a job at your company.

487
00:30:28,096 --> 00:30:29,576
I'm not going to stop you.

488
00:30:29,576 --> 00:30:31,976
But I'd like you to get experience
outside first.

489
00:30:32,976 --> 00:30:34,056
Kit,

490
00:30:34,056 --> 00:30:35,656
I'm grown up now.

491
00:30:35,656 --> 00:30:36,656
I'll prove it to you.

492
00:30:38,656 --> 00:30:40,976
That's what I'm talking about, my little brother.

493
00:30:45,016 --> 00:30:46,096
Then

494
00:30:46,816 --> 00:30:49,576
I will go back and make dinner for you.

495
00:30:52,016 --> 00:30:53,056
What are you going to cook?

496
00:30:53,056 --> 00:30:54,136
Not telling.

497
00:30:54,896 --> 00:30:56,136
But I guarantee you'll like it.

498
00:31:04,056 --> 00:31:05,776
You spoil me like this...

499
00:31:05,776 --> 00:31:06,816
it's really nice.

500
00:31:07,736 --> 00:31:08,736
I like it.

501
00:31:33,536 --> 00:31:35,056
Everything in this house

502
00:31:35,056 --> 00:31:36,296
has been arranged by Nont.

503
00:31:39,736 --> 00:31:41,216
The brands I use...

504
00:31:42,736 --> 00:31:44,136
the scents I like...

505
00:31:44,656 --> 00:31:45,896
how does Nont know all this?

506
00:32:45,736 --> 00:32:48,056
He didn't even forget about this one.

507
00:33:50,119 --> 00:33:51,279
Let's eat.

508
00:33:52,639 --> 00:33:54,279
Salmon, your favorite recipe.

509
00:33:56,399 --> 00:33:58,679
Salmon, grilled vegetables,
mashed potatoes.

510
00:33:58,679 --> 00:34:00,239
Under 500 calories total.

511
00:34:00,239 --> 00:34:01,719
Perfect for a day after a hard workout.

512
00:34:13,639 --> 00:34:14,519
Mmm.

513
00:34:15,559 --> 00:34:17,239
Then let me dry your hair for you.

514
00:34:18,239 --> 00:34:19,439
It's still wet.

515
00:34:19,439 --> 00:34:20,479
You'll get sick.

516
00:34:31,679 --> 00:34:32,599
Mmm.

517
00:34:33,199 --> 00:34:35,359
The weight of your hands is really nice.

518
00:34:35,879 --> 00:34:36,879
I like it.

519
00:34:37,479 --> 00:34:39,399
Right now my heart is beating so fast.

520
00:34:40,439 --> 00:34:41,919
Do you know, Kit?

521
00:34:42,639 --> 00:34:44,639
When was the first time

522
00:34:45,679 --> 00:34:47,279
I felt this way about you?

523
00:35:20,119 --> 00:35:21,719
I had a feeling you wouldn't be asleep yet.

524
00:35:31,999 --> 00:35:32,839
Here.

525
00:35:37,919 --> 00:35:38,879
Thank you.

526
00:35:41,679 --> 00:35:42,719
Are you okay?

527
00:35:48,759 --> 00:35:49,919
It's been a month now, Kit.

528
00:35:52,519 --> 00:35:53,759
I haven't been able to sleep at all.

529
00:35:57,199 --> 00:35:58,199
I know.

530
00:35:59,119 --> 00:36:00,919
That's why I came out to keep you company.

531
00:36:02,479 --> 00:36:03,999
It feels like it just happened yesterday.

532
00:36:09,119 --> 00:36:10,959
My parents were taking me on a trip.

533
00:36:14,319 --> 00:36:15,679
There were three of us.

534
00:36:18,119 --> 00:36:19,599
But when I opened my eyes...

535
00:36:22,399 --> 00:36:23,639
I had no one left.

536
00:36:32,359 --> 00:36:34,959
Your parents had to leave,

537
00:36:34,959 --> 00:36:36,439
even though they didn't want to.

538
00:36:37,799 --> 00:36:38,879
But in my case...

539
00:36:39,439 --> 00:36:40,999
my father chose to leave.

540
00:36:40,999 --> 00:36:42,079
He chose a new family

541
00:36:43,679 --> 00:36:46,119
and never came back to me
and my mom again.

542
00:36:56,279 --> 00:36:58,719
I'm sorry.

543
00:36:59,359 --> 00:37:01,439
I didn't mean to make you talk about it.

544
00:37:03,599 --> 00:37:05,079
Don't apologize.

545
00:37:05,559 --> 00:37:06,719
I just wanted you to know

546
00:37:07,199 --> 00:37:08,879
that our lives aren't that different.

547
00:37:10,399 --> 00:37:12,079
Back then, you might have had no one.

548
00:37:14,759 --> 00:37:15,959
But now, you have me.

549
00:37:20,039 --> 00:37:21,319
Thank you.

550
00:37:22,399 --> 00:37:23,879
For letting me stay with you...

551
00:37:25,399 --> 00:37:26,519
even though

552
00:37:27,279 --> 00:37:29,119
I'm not your real brother.

553
00:37:30,279 --> 00:37:31,679
We couldn't choose

554
00:37:31,679 --> 00:37:33,079
the life we've lived so far.

555
00:37:34,599 --> 00:37:36,039
But the life from here on

556
00:37:36,039 --> 00:37:37,719
we can choose to be happy.

557
00:37:52,399 --> 00:37:53,439
For me?

558
00:37:53,839 --> 00:37:55,839
Mm. Let's share.

559
00:38:13,039 --> 00:38:14,159
Nont.

560
00:38:14,159 --> 00:38:15,199
It's dry now.

561
00:38:16,079 --> 00:38:17,359
Oh.

562
00:38:17,359 --> 00:38:18,359
Right.

563
00:38:30,759 --> 00:38:31,799
Thanks.

564
00:38:33,719 --> 00:38:34,959
No need to thank me.

565
00:38:35,639 --> 00:38:36,799
I want to do it for you.

566
00:38:47,119 --> 00:38:48,399
How is it? Delicious?

567
00:38:49,079 --> 00:38:49,919
Delicious.

568
00:39:22,159 --> 00:39:24,639
Hello? This is Nontawat speaking.

569
00:39:24,639 --> 00:39:26,559
I'm calling from RC Company.

570
00:39:26,559 --> 00:39:27,919
Please come in for an interview

571
00:39:27,919 --> 00:39:29,399
tomorrow at 9 a.m.

572
00:39:29,399 --> 00:39:31,079
I'll be there on time.

573
00:39:31,079 --> 00:39:32,479
Thank you very much.

574
00:39:32,479 --> 00:39:33,719
See you then.

575
00:39:38,999 --> 00:39:40,479
RC Capital!

576
00:39:51,559 --> 00:39:52,999
I will prove to you...

577
00:39:54,719 --> 00:39:55,839
that I have grown up.

578
00:39:59,199 --> 00:40:00,599
And that I can be something more...

579
00:40:01,999 --> 00:40:03,599
than just a little brother.

580
00:40:19,079 --> 00:40:22,599
♪ I've never believed in love ♪

581
00:40:22,599 --> 00:40:25,999
♪ I've never trusted anyone ♪

582
00:40:25,999 --> 00:40:28,639
♪ I've always lived by reason ♪

583
00:40:28,639 --> 00:40:32,999
♪ I've never followed my heart ♪

584
00:40:32,999 --> 00:40:36,279
♪ Locked away with a complicated code ♪

585
00:40:36,279 --> 00:40:40,639
♪ But you broke through
My heavily guarded firewall ♪

586
00:40:40,639 --> 00:40:44,759
♪ That used to protect my heart ♪

587
00:40:45,839 --> 00:40:49,679
♪ I'm in love with you ♪

588
00:40:49,679 --> 00:40:53,279
♪ I've just realized today that love ♪

589
00:40:53,279 --> 00:40:59,319
♪ Is something I should get to know and explore ♪

590
00:40:59,319 --> 00:41:02,679
♪ The code to my heart has been cracked ♪

591
00:41:02,679 --> 00:41:06,679
♪ By the love you wrapped me in ♪

592
00:41:06,679 --> 00:41:09,599
♪ Having you close puts you in my dreams ♪

593
00:41:09,599 --> 00:41:10,879
♪ You're always on my mind ♪

594
00:41:10,879 --> 00:41:13,479
♪ You cracked my code ♪

595
00:41:13,479 --> 00:41:16,679
♪ My heart's security system is disabled ♪

596
00:41:16,679 --> 00:41:19,839
♪ You unlocked my heart with a love ♪

597
00:41:19,839 --> 00:41:24,039
♪ That this world has never given me ♪

598
00:42:32,425 --> 00:42:34,425
And every morning...

599
00:42:34,425 --> 00:42:36,945
you never hear what I say to you.

600
00:42:37,745 --> 00:42:39,305
Because I'm still not brave enough

601
00:42:39,305 --> 00:42:40,905
to let you hear it.

602
00:42:44,025 --> 00:42:45,225
I love you, Kit.

603
00:43:47,745 --> 00:43:48,865
I know...

604
00:43:49,585 --> 00:43:50,865
if I tell you directly

605
00:43:51,385 --> 00:43:52,825
without a good enough reason,

606
00:43:53,385 --> 00:43:54,265
you'll be angry.

607
00:43:54,985 --> 00:43:56,865
But if I can prove to you that

608
00:43:57,305 --> 00:43:58,705
I can get a job on my own,

609
00:43:59,665 --> 00:44:00,905
you'll change your mind.

610
00:44:17,825 --> 00:44:18,705
One day...

611
00:44:19,145 --> 00:44:20,305
you'll have to accept it.

612
00:44:20,745 --> 00:44:22,185
Then I won't have to take it off anymore.

613
00:44:47,945 --> 00:44:49,825
Nontawat Auttawarakul.

614
00:44:52,225 --> 00:44:54,385
First, let me ask you straight.

615
00:44:54,945 --> 00:44:56,945
What are you to Kittipat Auttawarakul?

616
00:44:58,105 --> 00:44:58,985
I'm his younger brother.

617
00:45:01,385 --> 00:45:02,465
Younger brother.

618
00:45:04,545 --> 00:45:07,025
Then why aren't you working
with your brother?

619
00:45:07,025 --> 00:45:09,785
Your brother's company is hot right now.

620
00:45:10,545 --> 00:45:13,065
Kit wanted me to get
experience elsewhere first.

621
00:45:15,345 --> 00:45:17,265
And does he know

622
00:45:17,265 --> 00:45:18,825
you're interviewing here?

623
00:45:19,265 --> 00:45:20,305
Not yet.

624
00:45:20,625 --> 00:45:21,745
Why not?

625
00:45:21,745 --> 00:45:23,305
I want to actually get the job first,

626
00:45:23,305 --> 00:45:24,585
then tell him.

627
00:45:25,465 --> 00:45:26,505
Good.

628
00:45:27,305 --> 00:45:29,705
I like people with a clear sense
of purpose like you.

629
00:45:30,545 --> 00:45:32,585
The position is Junior PR/Marketing.

630
00:45:32,585 --> 00:45:34,545
Do you think you can do it?

631
00:45:34,545 --> 00:45:35,945
Definitely.

632
00:45:35,945 --> 00:45:37,825
I majored in PR/Marketing directly

633
00:45:38,225 --> 00:45:39,465
both bachelor's and master's.

634
00:45:40,465 --> 00:45:42,465
But being skilled and being able
to actually do it

635
00:45:42,465 --> 00:45:43,985
are two different things.

636
00:45:43,985 --> 00:45:45,585
Give me a chance.

637
00:45:45,585 --> 00:45:48,105
I'll show you they're the same thing.

638
00:45:49,345 --> 00:45:50,225
Okay.

639
00:45:50,945 --> 00:45:53,105
Then I'll give you one test assignment.

640
00:45:53,785 --> 00:45:56,625
If you can do it, I'll hire you.

641
00:45:57,225 --> 00:45:59,785
And you can propose your own salary.

642
00:46:02,665 --> 00:46:03,825
Propose my own salary?

643
00:46:04,905 --> 00:46:06,185
Mm, yes.

644
00:46:07,625 --> 00:46:08,945
Because I believe people

645
00:46:09,425 --> 00:46:11,305
who know their own worth

646
00:46:11,625 --> 00:46:12,865
won't cheat themselves

647
00:46:12,865 --> 00:46:14,025
and won't cheat others.

648
00:46:16,145 --> 00:46:17,585
But if you fail the test,

649
00:46:18,545 --> 00:46:20,505
that's it. No second round.

650
00:46:20,985 --> 00:46:22,185
Deal?

651
00:46:22,905 --> 00:46:23,905
Deal.

652
00:46:25,265 --> 00:46:27,025
The test is a PR campaign

653
00:46:27,025 --> 00:46:28,865
for a new project.

654
00:46:29,385 --> 00:46:30,865
I'll send you the details tomorrow.

655
00:46:31,945 --> 00:46:33,065
You have three days.

656
00:46:34,105 --> 00:46:35,105
Understood.

657
00:46:42,505 --> 00:46:44,585
Nice to meet you, Mr. Nontawat.

658
00:46:46,025 --> 00:46:47,185
Likewise.

659
00:46:49,385 --> 00:46:50,825
Thank you for the opportunity.

660
00:46:51,785 --> 00:46:52,785
Yes.

661
00:47:06,585 --> 00:47:08,105
The younger brother,

662
00:47:08,105 --> 00:47:09,865
and he doesn't want his brother to know.

663
00:47:14,185 --> 00:47:16,585
Kit, I have a surprise for you.

664
00:47:16,585 --> 00:47:17,745
What surprise?

665
00:47:19,185 --> 00:47:21,505
So you don't agree with my approach.

666
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:22,985
I want to do it my way.

667
00:47:22,985 --> 00:47:24,945
I'll let Nont handle this campaign.

668
00:47:25,425 --> 00:47:27,785
I know Kit isn't happy
that I didn't listen to him.

669
00:47:27,785 --> 00:47:30,945
I hope this will make him see me differently

670
00:47:31,745 --> 00:47:33,465
not just as his younger brother.

671
00:47:37,745 --> 00:47:39,265
Where are we going?

672
00:47:39,265 --> 00:47:40,385
We're going to your room.

673
00:47:40,385 --> 00:47:43,545
No, I want to sleep with you.

674
00:47:46,385 --> 00:47:50,185
♪ When closeness starts to stir up feelings ♪

675
00:47:50,185 --> 00:47:57,385
♪ And my heart starts to get carried away ♪

676
00:47:57,385 --> 00:48:00,945
♪ As our bond begins to change ♪

677
00:48:00,945 --> 00:48:03,145
♪ Every time I look at you ♪

678
00:48:03,145 --> 00:48:05,505
♪ My heart ♪

679
00:48:05,945 --> 00:48:09,465
♪ Flutters more than I can bear ♪

680
00:48:09,865 --> 00:48:12,545
♪ Before I knew it ♪

681
00:48:12,545 --> 00:48:15,265
♪ Before I realized how I felt ♪

682
00:48:15,265 --> 00:48:18,585
♪ I couldn't stop it anymore ♪

683
00:48:18,585 --> 00:48:21,825
♪ It's too late now ♪

684
00:48:21,825 --> 00:48:27,465
♪ I'm already yours ♪

685
00:48:29,425 --> 00:48:32,785
♪ Somehow I gave my heart to you ♪

686
00:48:33,225 --> 00:48:38,985
♪ I don't even know when it happened ♪

687
00:48:40,185 --> 00:48:43,505
♪ Someone who's always here ♪

688
00:48:43,505 --> 00:48:48,465
♪ Someone you know so well ♪

689
00:48:48,945 --> 00:48:54,385
♪ There's something I've been waiting to say ♪

690
00:48:54,385 --> 00:48:59,825
♪ But I don't know how to say it ♪

691
00:49:02,025 --> 00:49:05,465
♪ Being by your side like this ♪

692
00:49:05,465 --> 00:49:09,625
♪ Makes me feel so good that I still... ♪
